      "topic": "actual Model",
      "result": "The Model expansion agrees with Def_FermatProperCarrier: K is an intermediate field ℚ≤K≤AlgebraicClosure(RatFunc ℚ), u is transcendental, u^N+v^N=1, ℚ(u,v)=K, and [K:ℚ(u)]=N with explicit finite_u. No actualModel selection or model-existence claim is added. N=0 is impossible under the equation in characteristic zero."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Place and all places",
      "result": "Place is exactly a proper valuation subring containing every rational. Divisors and inequalities quantify over this full carrier, including places at infinity, rather than one affine chart."
    },
    {
      "topic": "degree and constants",
      "result": "degree is the actual Module.finrank ℚ of the existing residue field. Residue finiteness follows from the curve-field dependency, not from a silently added constant-field equality. No assertion that the full algebraic constant field equals ℚ is introduced."
    },
    {
      "topic": "orders and zero",
      "result": "The two order definitions use the same maximal-ideal valuation; ord_eq_placeOrd is rfl. v_P(0)=0 is explicit, and function, zero, and pole divisors at zero all vanish. Division identity retains both nonzero hypotheses."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Riemann–Roch finrank",
      "result": "L(A) is the actual rational subspace with its separate zero clause and inequalities at every place. finrank has natural-number value zero in infinite dimension. Both lower-bound declarations retain hFinite for every divisor, even though their proofs instantiate it only at the target space."
    },
    {
      "topic": "fixed basis correction",
      "result": "The lower-bound readbacks use the existing functionBasis from Module.finBasis over ℚ(u), indexed by Fin(finrank), and the exact sum of its pole divisors; no arbitrary substitute correction or equality claim is inserted."
