      "result": "Each instance has exactly {K}[Field K][CharZero K](t), plus the stated ideal I for quotient instances. IsCurveField, Fact(Transcendental), Model, and finite-dimensionality binders are absent. chartRatAlgebra selects (chartRing t).algebra'; quotient instances select Ideal.Quotient.algebra ℚ; chartFaithfulSMul proves the canonical R_t action faithful from the inclusion into K."
    },
    {
      "topic": "inertia terminology",
      "result": "The existing Chinese term 惯性次数 is retained. Here it denotes the finrank of the corresponding residue-field extension, the same mathematical degree often called 剩余次数. Because R_t/(t_R) has rational finrank one, the equality specializes this degree to finrank_ℚ(A_t/𝔭). No curve-field or finite-dimensionality binder is added; infinite-dimensional finrank is zero."
